---
import NavHeader from '../components/NavHeader.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import '../styles/base.css';

// Page metadata
const title = 'Content Policy | Stories From The Web';
const description = 'Our content policy outlines the standards and guidelines for all content published on Stories From The Web, ensuring a safe and positive environment for young readers.';
---

<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
    <meta name="generator" content={Astro.generator} />
    <title>{title}</title>
    <meta name="description" content={description} />
  </head>
  <body class="min-h-screen flex flex-col bg-neutral-50 text-text-primary font-sans">
    <NavHeader />
    
    <main class="flex-grow w-full">
      <div class="container mx-auto px-4 py-8 max-w-4xl">
        <header class="mb-8 text-center">
          <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold text-text-primary mb-4">
            Content Policy
          </h1>
          <p class="text-xl text-text-secondary">
            Our commitment to providing a safe and positive environment
          </p>
        </header>

        <div class="bg-white rounded-xl shadow-md p-8 mb-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">Our Content Philosophy</h2>
          <p class="mb-4">
            At Stories From The Web, we believe that children deserve access to high-quality, 
            age-appropriate content that inspires creativity, fosters empathy, and encourages 
            a love of reading. Our content policy is designed to ensure that all stories on our 
            platform align with these values and provide a safe, positive experience for young readers.
          </p>
          <p>
            We welcome diverse perspectives and creative expression, while maintaining strict 
            standards to protect our young audience. This policy applies to all content published 
            on our platform, including stories, comments, profiles, and images.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-white rounded-xl shadow-md p-8 mb-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">Prohibited Content</h2>
          <p class="mb-4">
            The following types of content are strictly prohibited on Stories From The Web:
          </p>
          
          <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-2">Inappropriate Content for Children</h3>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mb-6 space-y-2">
            <li>Explicit or implied sexual content of any kind</li>
            <li>Graphic violence, gore, or horror elements</li>
            <li>Profanity or crude language</li>
            <li>Promotion of adult themes inappropriate for children under 13</li>
            <li>Content that may cause significant fear or distress in young readers</li>
          </ul>
          
          <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-2">Harmful or Dangerous Content</h3>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mb-6 space-y-2">
            <li>Promotion of dangerous activities that children might imitate</li>
            <li>Content encouraging self-harm, eating disorders, or other harmful behaviors</li>
            <li>Glorification of risky behaviors (e.g., running away from home)</li>
            <li>Instructions for dangerous pranks or challenges</li>
            <li>Promotion of substance use (including alcohol, tobacco, or drugs)</li>
          </ul>
          
          <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-2">Discriminatory or Hateful Content</h3>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mb-6 space-y-2">
            <li>Content that promotes discrimination, prejudice, or stereotypes</li>
            <li>Hateful content targeting individuals or groups based on protected characteristics</li>
            <li>Bullying, harassment, or content that normalizes these behaviors</li>
            <li>Content that demeans or belittles others</li>
          </ul>
          
          <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-2">Misleading or Deceptive Content</h3>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mb-6 space-y-2">
            <li>Misinformation or factually incorrect educational content</li>
            <li>Content that blurs the line between fact and fiction without clear indication</li>
            <li>Deceptive content designed to confuse or mislead children</li>
          </ul>
          
          <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-2">Privacy and Safety Concerns</h3>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mb-6 space-y-2">
            <li>Content containing personal information of minors</li>
            <li>Stories that could be used to identify or locate a specific child</li>
            <li>Content encouraging children to share personal information</li>
          </ul>
          
          <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-2">Copyright and Intellectual Property</h3>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mb-6 space-y-2">
            <li>Plagiarized content or unauthorized use of others' work</li>
            <li>Unauthorized use of copyrighted characters, settings, or storylines</li>
            <li>Content that infringes on trademarks or other intellectual property rights</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-white rounded-xl shadow-md p-8 mb-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">Content Moderation Process</h2>
          
          <p class="mb-4">
            All content submitted to Stories From The Web undergoes a moderation process to ensure 
            compliance with our content policy:
          </p>
          
          <ol class="list-decimal pl-6 mb-6 space-y-4">
            <li>
              <strong>Initial Submission</strong>
              <p>Authors submit their stories through our publishing platform.</p>
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Automated Screening</strong>
              <p>Our system performs an initial automated check for prohibited content.</p>
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Human Review</strong>
              <p>Our moderation team reviews each submission to ensure it meets our content standards.</p>
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Feedback</strong>
              <p>If content doesn't meet our standards, we provide feedback to the author explaining why.</p>
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Publication or Revision</strong>
              <p>Content that meets our standards is published; otherwise, authors can revise and resubmit.</p>
            </li>
          </ol>
          
          <p>
            We strive to complete the moderation process within 1-3 business days of submission.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-white rounded-xl shadow-md p-8 mb-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">Reporting Inappropriate Content</h2>
          
          <p class="mb-4">
            If you encounter content that violates our policy, please report it immediately:
          </p>
          
          <ol class="list-decimal pl-6 mb-6 space-y-2">
            <li>Use the "Report" button available on all content pages</li>
            <li>Provide specific details about why you believe the content violates our policy</li>
            <li>Our moderation team will review all reports within 24-48 hours</li>
            <li>If the content is found to violate our policy, it will be removed promptly</li>
          </ol>
          
          <p>
            We take all reports seriously and appreciate your help in maintaining a safe environment.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-white rounded-xl shadow-md p-8 mb-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">Policy Updates</h2>
          
          <p class="mb-4">
            Our content policy may be updated periodically to address emerging issues or improve clarity. 
            When significant changes are made, we will notify our community through:
          </p>
          
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mb-6 space-y-2">
            <li>Announcements on our website</li>
            <li>Email notifications to registered users</li>
            <li>Updates to this policy page with the date of revision</li>
          </ul>
          
          <p>
            It is the responsibility of all users to stay informed about our current content policy.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="text-center mt-8">
          <p class="text-lg mb-4">Questions about our content policy?</p>
          <a href="/contact" class="inline-block bg-primary text-white px-6 py-3 rounded-lg font-semibold hover:bg-primary-dark transition-colors">
            Contact Us
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </main>
    
    <Footer />
  </body>
</html>
